          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em braided monoidal functor
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : C \to D
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braided+monoidal+categories"} braided monoidal categories
            that is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            which respects the braiding on both sides, i.e. satisfies the law:
          %svg{:height => "105.076pt", :version => "1.2", :viewbox => "0 0 298.157 105.076", :width => "298.157pt", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/2000/svg", "xmlns:xlink" => "http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"}
